WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.580
This has been a chaotic

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.930
and emotionally wrenching week in America.

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:07.320
And so we've been dedicating
our television time

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.260
to conversations with people

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.010
who really understand what it's like

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:14.550
to be Black in America in 2020.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:15.780
Earlier today,

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.500
I had a great talk with
my very talented friend,

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.450
Sam Richardson.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:22.210
So let's go to that now.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.380
My guest tonight flew
across the world last year

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:28.010
to introduce me to the country of Ghana.

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:29.400
And it's incredible people.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.700
He's a very talented comedian

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.590
who starred on the
acclaimed HBO series "Veep".

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:37.460
as well as the Comedy
Central series "Detroiters".

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.990
And I'm so glad he's with me tonight.

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:41.490
Please welcome a really good friend,

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:43.600
Sam Richardson.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:44.700
Hey Sam.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:45.750
Hey Conan.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.830
Thanks very much for being here.

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:51.920
I know that you would express
a little bit of concern

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.010
or maybe trepidation

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.540
about coming on tonight.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:55.690
Is that true or...

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:56.560
Well yeah.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.883
'Cause personally,

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:02.540
I feel there's people

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:05.390
who are more eloquent in expressing

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:07.590
what's happening

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:09.110
or better...

00:01:11.612 --> 00:01:16.036
A figurehead for the responsibility

00:01:16.036 --> 00:01:19.490
of expressing what's going on right now.

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:21.000
Right.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.970
But ultimately it came to the decision.

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:25.290
Well you know,

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:27.400
I am a Black man in America,

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:32.400
so I have empirical
knowledge of the situation,

00:01:33.249 --> 00:01:35.730
and all I can do is speak for myself.

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:38.340
And you are my friend,

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:42.840
and I appreciate your idea

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.380
of raising Black voices to speak.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:49.220
So I figured this was a
good opportunity to do that.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:52.330
Yeah. I think there doesn't need to be...

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:54.890
I know what you mean,

00:01:54.890 --> 00:01:56.140
'cause there are many times

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:59.540
when all of us in different
situations feel inadequate.

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:00.560
I'm constantly thinking,

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.670
why am I talking?

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:03.830
Not just in this situation,

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:05.740
but in a lot of situations.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:07.300
And then I think,

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:08.710
this isn't just about people

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:13.640
who are specialists in Black history

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:15.963
or Black history in America.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.030
It's not just about them.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:21.240
It's about everybody who
has something to say,

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:24.270
who's experienced firsthand
what this is like.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:26.140
So how are you?

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:29.307
How are you as a human being right now?

00:02:29.307 --> 00:02:30.429
(laughs) Well I mean,

00:02:30.429 --> 00:02:33.423
that's the question, right?

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:35.580
Every phone call,

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:36.413
every meeting,

00:02:36.413 --> 00:02:37.420
every thing will start with that.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:42.420
And it's like a really
double Dutch kinda answer.

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:45.273
Fact of the matter,

00:02:45.273 --> 00:02:47.270
I'm incredibly sad.

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:48.973
I'm incredibly angry.

00:02:51.633 --> 00:02:56.633
But at the same time I'd say,

00:02:56.730 --> 00:03:00.030
I'm not surprised.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:05.030
And I think no Black person
in America is surprised

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:08.360
or shocked by what's happening

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:09.290
or what's happened.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.200
We've known this whole time.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.830
I think what is...

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:15.750
I don't even know if I wanna
use the word encouraging.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:16.583
But what is encouraging,

00:03:16.583 --> 00:03:20.390
is watching the actual reaction to it.

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:24.960
Thing that has been happening for ever.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:25.990
But now it's a time

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:29.380
where there's a solid fight back.

00:03:29.380 --> 00:03:33.350
So that is an encouraging thing.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:35.078
But I'm perfectly,

00:03:35.078 --> 00:03:36.450
I'm sad all the time,

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:37.370
I'm mad all the time,

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:38.860
I'm filled with anxiety.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:40.818
And I watch (laughs)...

00:03:40.818 --> 00:03:42.840
I can't keep off my phone

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.580
from seeing what's going on.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:46.117
But at the same time I try

00:03:46.117 --> 00:03:49.330
and just take care of myself.

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:51.253
And that's what we need to do.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.690
I can't let myself get into full despair,

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:00.650
I've to let myself get into action.

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:02.440
That makes sense.
Right.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:03.563
It does make sense.

00:04:06.611 --> 00:04:10.860
I'm curious because you and
I went a year ago to Ghana,

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.896
you showed me your country

00:04:13.896 --> 00:04:17.120
that your family is from.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:21.890
You have this really fascinating worldview

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:25.470
because you come from two worlds.

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:28.200
You've spent time growing up in Ghana,

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.363
but also Detroit.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:36.140
And so you have this perspective

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:38.980
that is to me absolutely unique.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:41.470
And maybe we could learn from.

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:42.930
Well yeah, it's true.

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:44.530
I grew up between two places.

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:48.130
I grew up between Ghana and Detroit.

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:49.960
And like in Ghana,

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:51.420
the faces are all black.

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:53.260
So I have no fear of being...

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:56.940
Of prejudice for this
color of my skin there.

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:00.770
Black people represent the wealthy elite,

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:02.320
the middle class

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:04.530
and the lower class there.

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:05.363
So,

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:07.860
that experience I have,

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:09.060
and then to juxtapose that

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:12.210
to my life in the United States,

00:05:12.210 --> 00:05:15.010
there is no bolder contrast to know that,

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:18.423
here legitimately it's
second-class citizen.

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:21.290
Have you talked to your mom?

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:24.640
Does she have a take on
what's happening right now?

00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:26.861
My mom is in Ghana right now,

00:05:26.861 --> 00:05:27.861
as a matter of fact.

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:32.301
And she's been quarantined
up and sequestered

00:05:32.301 --> 00:05:33.710
because of COVID and everything.

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:37.250
And the borders are closed there still.

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:41.830
But she's just worried
about my safety being here.

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:43.790
She's nervous and she's frightened.

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:46.130
And my dad is in Detroit right now.

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:47.623
Same sentiments.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:51.970
The fear that exists.

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:52.870
And I'm not a parent,

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:56.267
but the fear that exists for parents

00:05:56.267 --> 00:06:01.117
to have your children
navigating the world.

00:06:01.117 --> 00:06:06.117
Where you know there is
a threat to their lives

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:09.233
and their livelihoods.

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:11.643
You know that's it.

00:06:11.643 --> 00:06:13.780
That's just it's reality.

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:15.360
Can you tell me what your experience

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:16.756
was specifically?

00:06:16.756 --> 00:06:17.589
I mean,

00:06:17.589 --> 00:06:18.453
I will tell you one of 'em.

00:06:19.747 --> 00:06:22.993
I remember I was at my girlfriend's house.

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:27.080
This is in Detroit suburbs,

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:28.850
this is in Berkeley.

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:31.090
And it was late night,

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:35.620
a drunk driver outside hit a pole.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:36.453
Hit it,

00:06:36.453 --> 00:06:39.120
crashed it right next to my car.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.360
The police came
investigating and I said...

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:43.030
I went out side and I was like,

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:44.050
oh, officers.

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:46.562
And the guy screamed at me so quick,

00:06:46.562 --> 00:06:47.649
Get the (beep) back!

00:06:47.649 --> 00:06:48.830
Get the (beep) back!

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:50.120
And handled the gun.

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:53.270
And maybe in that instant,

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:58.270
I had forgotten what the protocol is

00:06:58.510 --> 00:07:00.770
for Black people dealing with police.

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:02.270
'Cause I was like trying to help,

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:04.730
like curious to see what
was going on with my car

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:06.430
that was right next to this thing.

00:07:11.416 --> 00:07:14.570
As if there was like a
bank robbery happening.

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:17.950
You came here for a drunk driver.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:18.800
Yeah, yeah.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:20.150
And a bystander.

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:22.023
What do you think my plan was?

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:27.090
And I remember I called my dad.

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:27.923
I had nothing.

00:07:27.923 --> 00:07:29.660
I didn't know what else to do.

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:31.350
I was just like F it, I called my dad.

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:32.183
He was like,

00:07:32.183 --> 00:07:33.040
yeah, remember.

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:34.593
And he said, remember.

00:07:36.544 --> 00:07:40.650
Another time I was much younger.

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:43.723
And I went into a sporting goods store,

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:46.570
Sports Authority.

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:48.380
And I was walking through the aisles

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:50.363
and just looking around perusing.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:54.960
I went to walk out of the Sports Authority

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:57.150
and this woman grabs me

00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:58.440
and yanked me into this room.

00:07:58.440 --> 00:07:59.740
She said, I know what you did.

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:00.573
I know what you did.

00:08:00.573 --> 00:08:01.650
The cops are coming,

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:02.483
the cops are coming.

00:08:02.483 --> 00:08:03.316
I know what you did.

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:07.890
And then the police showed up

00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:08.723
and they were like,

00:08:08.723 --> 00:08:10.010
we know that you stole something.

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:11.860
And I just couldn't...

00:08:13.311 --> 00:08:18.311
(laughs) I was just fully confused.

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:19.153
You know,

00:08:19.153 --> 00:08:20.483
I'm like 12 years old.

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:24.910
It's threat.

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:26.450
But this woman was like,

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:28.170
oh, I can...

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:32.630
This boy must've stole something.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:33.730
And I have the proof of it

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:36.740
and I'm going to directly
get it out of him.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:39.370
The police come and they're as aggressive.

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:41.090
They checked the footage

00:08:42.150 --> 00:08:44.490
of me in the aisle way.

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:48.490
And I had taken off my watch

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:50.710
to put on a baseball glove

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:52.803
and put my watch in my pocket.

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:58.270
And the response

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:01.393
as though I had committed
an armed robbery.

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:05.560
And she knew that calling the police

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:07.100
was going to elicit that sort of response.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:10.250
Like I had no quarter.

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:11.290
Wow, you're 12.

00:09:11.290 --> 00:09:12.232
You're 12 years old.

00:09:12.232 --> 00:09:13.080
12 years old.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:13.913
Yeah.

00:09:13.913 --> 00:09:15.390
This is in Dearborn, Michigan.

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:19.940
How do you contain that anger?

00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:21.333
Do you know what I'm saying?

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:28.000
This is from my perspective.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:32.143
But in all the time we spent together,

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:36.160
it's hard for me to imagine you containing

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:39.980
those infuriating humiliating experiences.

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:40.813
Do you know what I mean?

00:09:40.813 --> 00:09:45.290
And so now in this moment it can come out.

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:47.710
But what do you do with that?

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:49.600
How do you live in the world

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:50.830
with that kind of anger?

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:53.230
I mean we all have to.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:54.220
You know what I mean?

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:57.361
If we were all to show the amount

00:09:57.361 --> 00:10:01.810
of frustration and fear that we feel,

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:04.303
we wouldn't be able to exist in society.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:08.017
I mean to make it nerd (laughs).

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:11.217
In the movie "Avengers",

00:10:13.833 --> 00:10:17.242
they're surrounded by the villains.

00:10:17.242 --> 00:10:19.430
The aliens are attacking.

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:20.690
Captain America's like,

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:23.580
Hulk now would be a
good time to get angry.

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:24.810
And Hulk looks at him and says,

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:26.180
that's my secret Cap,

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:27.343
I'm always angry.

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:30.353
I'm always angry.

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:38.450
I can't let that anger make me...

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.020
I can't let that anger dictate my life

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:44.623
and stop me from experiencing life.

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:48.820
That's true for all of us.

00:10:48.820 --> 00:10:52.370
There's no way that we can
see what happens in the world.

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:57.370
And watch these cases
of violence against us

00:10:57.450 --> 00:11:00.033
and not be angry.

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:05.248
And these things boil over.

00:11:05.248 --> 00:11:06.560
What we're watching right now

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:08.653
is things boiling over.

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:12.623
I've been talking this week.

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:15.570
Trying to look for...

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:21.683
Trying to listen and also
trying to figure out.

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:26.180
How can this not be just another incident

00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:27.620
that we all process,

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:30.647
there's unrest and then we move on?

00:11:30.647 --> 00:11:32.970
You find yourselves back
in the same situation

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:33.880
six months from now,

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:35.890
two years from now.

00:11:35.890 --> 00:11:39.040
What's the way forward?

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:41.080
And one of the things

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:45.110
that W. Kamau Bell told me yesterday

00:11:45.110 --> 00:11:46.340
was he said it's action.

00:11:46.340 --> 00:11:47.573
Let's see your work.

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:51.250
And I thought that really spoke to me.

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:52.433
Which is,

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:57.040
yes there's a lot of talk
right now and talk is good.

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:58.490
And there are a lot of people

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:03.450
trying to symbolically,

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:06.090
and I'm talking about white people

00:12:06.090 --> 00:12:09.080
trying to show that they care.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:11.240
But then so much more about...

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:14.460
It feels like right now is about,

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:15.950
what are you going to do?

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:19.140
What are people going
to do moving forward?

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:20.570
What is your work?

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:22.610
And you gotta keep at it.

00:12:22.610 --> 00:12:27.610
Meaning there's clearly a
lot of work here to be done.

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:31.910
So I don't know if that's...

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:37.830
Well, I think right now
there's a sweet spot.

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:44.120
'Cause everybody's at home with COVID,

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:47.610
everybody's closed in
and are faced with it.

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:49.260
They have to see what's happening.

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:51.710
And there's not immediately
after a distraction.

00:12:51.710 --> 00:12:53.040
'Cause you know like,

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:55.470
go to work and then forget
about what's happening.

00:12:55.470 --> 00:12:57.760
If you're bombarded with it every day,

00:12:57.760 --> 00:12:58.680
you see what's happening,

00:12:58.680 --> 00:12:59.513
you see what's happening.

00:12:59.513 --> 00:13:01.913
It's impossible to ignore right now.

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:09.110
That shows that these things aren't new,

00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:10.540
but you can watch.

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:11.620
Like now everybody's watching

00:13:11.620 --> 00:13:14.540
and you just see how
close together they are

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:16.830
and that's constant.

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:18.380
These things didn't just start

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:20.820
when everybody was at home watching

00:13:20.820 --> 00:13:23.720
their phones and that.

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:25.230
But they're constant.

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:29.430
So now everybody is forced to act.

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:31.810
So like moving forward,

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:32.652
it has to be,

00:13:32.652 --> 00:13:33.485
everybody has to remember

00:13:33.485 --> 00:13:35.820
how they feel right now.

00:13:35.820 --> 00:13:38.370
Everybody has to act right now

00:13:38.370 --> 00:13:39.360
and do as much as they can.

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:40.290
People,

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:42.700
we want to be distracted as much as we can

00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:44.680
'cause we wanna keep our
world the same way it is

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:46.270
'cause we're comfortable in it.

00:13:46.270 --> 00:13:47.280
But right now,

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:48.400
people are uncomfortable

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:50.393
and have to remember that discomfort.

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:54.060
It's called the pain for change.

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:56.830
How much stress

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:59.450
or how much pain can
you put on a situation

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:01.093
before you have to change it?

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:07.000
Like if somebody's pinching you,

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:08.730
a person who gets pinched the second,

00:14:08.730 --> 00:14:09.780
this pinch doesn't mean anything.

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:10.950
So you don't move.

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.110
And somebody pinches harder,

00:14:12.110 --> 00:14:12.943
you don't do this.

00:14:12.943 --> 00:14:13.776
Somebody pinches hard you say,

00:14:13.776 --> 00:14:14.609
Ow stop it!

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:17.700
Then you change your circumstances.

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:18.533
So right now,

00:14:18.533 --> 00:14:20.700
we have to remember this pain

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:23.860
before all the other distractions
of the world come in.

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:24.693
And we're watching.

00:14:24.693 --> 00:14:26.670
We're watching things are happening.

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:28.793
All four officers have been charged.

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:35.140
The Breonna Taylor case has been reopened.

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:37.210
We're watching these things happen.

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:39.530
And then we keep on it,

00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:42.130
we can effect real change.

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:43.420
And that's another thing too,

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:45.140
it's up to white people

00:14:45.140 --> 00:14:48.273
and all people to educate themselves.

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:51.010
The knee jerk reaction

00:14:51.010 --> 00:14:53.010
of when somebody says Black lives matter

00:14:53.010 --> 00:14:54.970
to then say all lives matter,

00:14:54.970 --> 00:14:56.590
whether you are well-intentioned

00:14:56.590 --> 00:14:59.500
or actively trying to discredit

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:01.470
the idea of Black lives matter.

00:15:01.470 --> 00:15:03.070
Pay attention to what that is.

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:03.903
You know what,

00:15:03.903 --> 00:15:05.180
what is it that makes you say that?

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:06.660
Do you really believe

00:15:06.660 --> 00:15:08.960
that when a person says
Black lives matter,

00:15:08.960 --> 00:15:11.470
we're saying Black lives matter more?

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:16.470
Or is it that the idea of
changing the system frightens you?

00:15:19.635 --> 00:15:20.790
I mean these are the questions

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:21.920
you gotta ask.

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:24.460
There's nothing more frustrating truly

00:15:24.460 --> 00:15:25.530
than going through your comments

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:27.600
or going through my comments

00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:28.433
and I say something Black lives matter,

00:15:28.433 --> 00:15:29.266
someone say,

00:15:29.266 --> 00:15:30.253
well all lives matter.

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:33.460
Hey, but don't you think we know that?

00:15:33.460 --> 00:15:35.030
Nobody said all lives don't matter.

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:37.160
Not once did I say a
white life doesn't matter.

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:38.960
Not once did I say any
life doesn't matter.

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:41.717
All I said is a Black life matters.

00:15:41.717 --> 00:15:43.148
Matters.

00:15:43.148 --> 00:15:44.173
Was it Michael Che?

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:46.717
In the stand up is like,

00:15:46.717 --> 00:15:48.430
At least we're starting out at "matters."

00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:53.150
That's the lowest talking point.

00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:55.993
And to see opposition to that?

00:15:58.050 --> 00:15:59.610
It's frustrating.

00:15:59.610 --> 00:16:00.443
Yeah.

00:16:03.589 --> 00:16:05.400
There's a fear of...

00:16:08.210 --> 00:16:09.660
People wanna,

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:11.453
and again I'm gonna be specific.

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:15.810
White Americans want to do things

00:16:15.810 --> 00:16:18.160
that will help

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:20.880
or make a difference

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:24.500
or sound like or be supportive.

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.200
And they might get it wrong.

00:16:26.200 --> 00:16:28.360
And then they might get checked for it.

00:16:28.360 --> 00:16:32.561
They may put up the...

00:16:32.561 --> 00:16:34.770
Like with the internet,

00:16:34.770 --> 00:16:37.390
people putting up the black tiles

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:38.830
thinking that...

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:41.400
And it's well intentioned.

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:45.920
But then it turns out to
actually not be helping

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:48.400
and angering some people.

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:49.550
And then there's a feeling

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:50.383
of well wait,

00:16:50.383 --> 00:16:51.240
I just touched the stove.

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:53.290
I thought I was helping and I got burned.

00:16:54.670 --> 00:16:57.900
One of the things that I've
been learning this week

00:16:57.900 --> 00:16:59.337
is yeah,

00:16:59.337 --> 00:17:00.770
be wrong.

00:17:00.770 --> 00:17:01.603
Try.

00:17:01.603 --> 00:17:06.030
Just keep trying and being embarrassed

00:17:06.030 --> 00:17:06.863
or saying,

00:17:06.863 --> 00:17:07.696
okay my bad.

00:17:07.696 --> 00:17:09.130
I thought this was the right thing to do,

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:09.963
it's not.

00:17:09.963 --> 00:17:11.860
Now I'm going to try again.

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:13.373
But my embarrassment,

00:17:14.430 --> 00:17:18.130
is a tiny, tiny, tiny
(laughs) price to pay.

00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:19.873
It's less than a mosquito bite.

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:25.690
This idea that people are
going to try something,

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:27.040
get checked for it online

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:28.910
and then get angry and say,

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:30.000
well I tried.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:30.833
Shut off.

00:17:30.833 --> 00:17:31.910
I put up a black tile

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:33.800
and now it turns out I'm
not supposed to do that.

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:37.737
So I'm out and I'm gonna
go watch "Real Housewives".

00:17:37.737 --> 00:17:40.040
(laughs) 'cause I tried
to help and that's that.

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:41.220
Well they don't want my help.

00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:42.053
So that's that,

00:17:42.053 --> 00:17:42.886
I'm done.

00:17:42.886 --> 00:17:43.719
Yeah.

00:17:43.719 --> 00:17:48.320
What education do you go in
knowing everything about it?

00:17:48.320 --> 00:17:50.030
What person goes into college,

00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:52.600
knowing everything about
the college courses?

00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:54.650
This is the time where
people are trying to learn,

00:17:54.650 --> 00:17:56.080
people need to learn.

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:58.330
So part of learning is
getting things wrong

00:17:58.330 --> 00:17:59.350
and then checking yourself

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:01.723
and then applying that to the next time.

00:18:04.528 --> 00:18:06.710
I always say people can't let

00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:08.700
their fear of getting things wrong,

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:11.450
or fear of not being able
to do the perfect thing,

00:18:11.450 --> 00:18:12.880
or getting things perfectly right,

00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:14.983
stop them from trying to do something.

00:18:15.950 --> 00:18:17.260
Those are the steps that you have to take.

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:19.210
You have to get out there

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:22.150
and just make the first step at least.

00:18:22.150 --> 00:18:23.510
And then let that encourage you to see.

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:24.343
Oh okay,

00:18:24.343 --> 00:18:25.530
I can do something.

00:18:25.530 --> 00:18:26.873
And then do the next step.

00:18:27.856 --> 00:18:29.006
And then the next step.

00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:33.570
People get the idea in their head

00:18:33.570 --> 00:18:34.940
that they need to just go straight

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:37.460
into being Martin Luther
King or Malcolm X.

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:39.706
And just from zero to 100.

00:18:39.706 --> 00:18:41.670
That's not rational.

00:18:41.670 --> 00:18:44.540
But you need to do something

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:47.000
and then learn from it and grow from it.

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:47.833
The growth,

00:18:47.833 --> 00:18:49.263
we have to grow in this.

00:18:50.420 --> 00:18:51.290
To back up,

00:18:51.290 --> 00:18:53.490
you took me to Ghana

00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:55.970
for us to do a special

00:18:55.970 --> 00:18:57.700
about "The Year of the Return",

00:18:57.700 --> 00:19:02.700
the 400 years since the first slave ships

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:06.850
were leaving Africa.

00:19:06.850 --> 00:19:11.600
And we went to Ghana to
experience that moment.

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:16.600
And we ran into this group

00:19:16.950 --> 00:19:21.100
of people from the Chicago,

00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:23.610
I think it's Trinity United Church.

00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:27.900
And they were all from Chicago

00:19:27.900 --> 00:19:31.130
and they were visiting

00:19:31.130 --> 00:19:34.280
to experience this moment.

00:19:34.280 --> 00:19:35.980
And I think it was Kumasi.

00:19:35.980 --> 00:19:37.100
Kumasi, yeah.

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:37.933
Yeah.

00:19:37.933 --> 00:19:41.240
And I started talking to them

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:43.170
and it was beautiful.

00:19:43.170 --> 00:19:45.110
They were so fantastic.

00:19:45.110 --> 00:19:49.210
And so moving to speak
to that I wanna make sure

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:50.560
we show that clip

00:19:50.560 --> 00:19:52.670
because this is from a year ago.

00:19:52.670 --> 00:19:54.683
But I think it resonates now.

00:19:56.270 --> 00:19:58.750
Probably more than it did then.

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:00.250
Why is it important for you to be here?

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:02.270
You know it's a time to remember those

00:20:02.270 --> 00:20:04.400
who came before us and our ancestors.

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:06.550
This is really deep to
see those who resisted.

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:07.383
That's a major thing.

00:20:07.383 --> 00:20:09.080
They bring up those who are resistors,

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:10.537
who fought back.

00:20:10.537 --> 00:20:11.910
And a lot of people did not make it.

00:20:11.910 --> 00:20:14.320
So many people died on his journey

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:16.430
to be shipped and taken from their home.

00:20:16.430 --> 00:20:17.263
All right.

00:20:17.263 --> 00:20:18.470
It's kind of an awakening.

00:20:18.470 --> 00:20:21.620
We've only been free
for roughly 160 years,

00:20:21.620 --> 00:20:24.340
whereas we've been in
bondage for over 400 years.

00:20:24.340 --> 00:20:26.220
So physically, yes.

00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:27.620
We're free mentally,

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:29.380
not so much.

00:20:29.380 --> 00:20:30.819
For me personally,

00:20:30.819 --> 00:20:32.680
I'm realizing how much racial stress

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:34.760
I'm under every day in America.

00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:36.590
I don't even realize it.

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:38.530
I don't even realize that
when I walk into spaces

00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:39.960
where I am in minority,

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:41.550
I am constantly checking myself.

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:43.030
Here, I don't feel that.

00:20:43.030 --> 00:20:43.863
When I am here,

00:20:43.863 --> 00:20:46.410
I feel that I am at home.

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:48.320
One thing that is striking

00:20:48.320 --> 00:20:51.260
is 400 years of slavery.

00:20:51.260 --> 00:20:52.750
Think about it,

00:20:52.750 --> 00:20:53.870
400 years.

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:56.063
How many generations of people,

00:20:57.060 --> 00:20:59.960
good people that sat on the sidelines

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:01.623
and watch slavery occur.

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:05.100
This is a lesson that we all need to learn

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:07.120
is that if we see injustice,

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:09.260
whether it's happening to us personally,

00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:12.420
or happening to our neighbors,

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:15.660
we gotta find a way to
speak out and stand up.

00:21:15.660 --> 00:21:17.120
And one thing that's on my mind,

00:21:17.120 --> 00:21:18.850
was one of the guys,

00:21:18.850 --> 00:21:21.930
that when we went back to one
of the slave auction castles,

00:21:21.930 --> 00:21:25.770
he said that you can either be bitter,

00:21:25.770 --> 00:21:27.700
which means you can leave here weak,

00:21:27.700 --> 00:21:29.400
or you can either be better,

00:21:29.400 --> 00:21:31.620
which means you'll leave here stronger.

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:33.809
And so I thought about what that meant.

00:21:33.809 --> 00:21:34.642
And what that meant

00:21:34.642 --> 00:21:36.060
is that we've seen much agony

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:37.080
and we've seen much pain,

00:21:37.080 --> 00:21:38.770
but we've also seen much hope

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:41.180
and much promise and much glory.

00:21:41.180 --> 00:21:43.270
So we must tell the whole story.

00:21:43.270 --> 00:21:45.220
But let us put as much emphasis

00:21:45.220 --> 00:21:48.160
on the hope and on the glory

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:50.660
and on the optimism as we tell the story

00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:51.493
so that people can say,

00:21:51.493 --> 00:21:54.000
well there is a better day.

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:55.410
You know how eloquent

00:21:55.410 --> 00:21:59.770
and how smart and on target
everybody was in that circle.

00:21:59.770 --> 00:22:02.190
Everybody had a...

00:22:02.190 --> 00:22:03.420
It was absurd.

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:06.750
A random group of I don't know

00:22:06.750 --> 00:22:10.270
if it was 20 or 25 people.

00:22:10.270 --> 00:22:14.040
I'd be hard pressed to
go anywhere in the world

00:22:14.040 --> 00:22:17.720
and grab 25 people and
ask them all their opinion

00:22:17.720 --> 00:22:19.373
and not one of them.

00:22:20.280 --> 00:22:21.840
Not one of them was anything less

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:25.450
than this beautifully
eloquent and powerful

00:22:25.450 --> 00:22:26.304
and (both laughing)

00:22:26.304 --> 00:22:28.991
(laughing drowns out
speaker) teleprompter.

00:22:28.991 --> 00:22:31.658
(both laughing)

00:22:34.120 --> 00:22:35.233
Where is the prompter?

00:22:36.330 --> 00:22:37.163
Absolutely.

00:22:38.530 --> 00:22:40.873
Such a beautiful moment and ...

00:22:45.120 --> 00:22:45.953
Every,

00:22:47.197 --> 00:22:48.380
it's hard to say every.

00:22:48.380 --> 00:22:49.490
But Black people,

00:22:49.490 --> 00:22:51.160
we experience the world,

00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:54.250
and we must be knowledgeable of it.

00:22:54.250 --> 00:22:56.390
And so you caught 25 people

00:22:56.390 --> 00:22:59.770
who are in a journey for knowledge.

00:22:59.770 --> 00:23:02.410
So every one of them has been thinking

00:23:02.410 --> 00:23:05.710
and expressing their
ideas so specifically.

00:23:05.710 --> 00:23:09.810
And cultivating what their feelings are.

00:23:09.810 --> 00:23:12.710
And so you caught them
at the perfect time.

00:23:12.710 --> 00:23:15.340
Because as a Black person,

00:23:15.340 --> 00:23:17.320
you have to be a scholar

00:23:17.320 --> 00:23:19.440
in order to understand your feelings

00:23:19.440 --> 00:23:22.647
of what's happening to you,

00:23:22.647 --> 00:23:24.820
and what's happening to
your people in this country

00:23:24.820 --> 00:23:26.113
for 400 years.

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:30.694
It's hard to ignore.

00:23:30.694 --> 00:23:34.160
So like those 25 people,

00:23:34.160 --> 00:23:37.243
you caught a sweet spot.

00:23:39.210 --> 00:23:40.620
You know this is,

00:23:40.620 --> 00:23:41.453
like I say,

00:23:46.910 --> 00:23:51.610
it must be endlessly frustrating to have,

00:23:51.610 --> 00:23:52.960
because this week,

00:23:52.960 --> 00:23:54.660
I've been talking to either it's Van Jones

00:23:54.660 --> 00:23:56.253
or W. Kamau Bell or you,

00:23:58.803 --> 00:24:01.150
that this incident happens

00:24:01.150 --> 00:24:02.860
and then suddenly everyone's asking you,

00:24:02.860 --> 00:24:04.760
how do you feel and educate me.

00:24:04.760 --> 00:24:07.800
Which is exhausting and not your job.

00:24:07.800 --> 00:24:09.480
It's not your job to educate us.

00:24:09.480 --> 00:24:11.453
It's our job to educate ourselves.

00:24:17.580 --> 00:24:19.450
Of everyone I've spoken to this week,

00:24:19.450 --> 00:24:21.000
you're the one I know the best.

00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:26.000
And it's upsetting to hear your stories.

00:24:26.381 --> 00:24:28.890
And because I know you

00:24:28.890 --> 00:24:33.030
to be such an amazingly
sweet and sensitive person.

00:24:33.030 --> 00:24:38.030
And I hate that 12 year
old or 20 year old you,

00:24:38.060 --> 00:24:38.893
or 30 year old you,

00:24:38.893 --> 00:24:40.390
had to go through any of that.

00:24:42.700 --> 00:24:43.960
It makes me nauseous,

00:24:43.960 --> 00:24:44.947
to be honest.

00:24:46.555 --> 00:24:47.720
So you know me,

00:24:47.720 --> 00:24:50.480
and this is just like a grand lesson

00:24:50.480 --> 00:24:52.600
for anybody who's watching or anything.

00:24:52.600 --> 00:24:53.650
You know me,

00:24:53.650 --> 00:24:56.040
and you'd know that I
have this experience.

00:24:56.040 --> 00:24:59.668
Imagine that for every
Black person that you know.

00:24:59.668 --> 00:25:01.070
Yeah.

00:25:01.070 --> 00:25:02.650
Whether you know them better than me,

00:25:02.650 --> 00:25:04.040
or you know them less than me,

00:25:04.040 --> 00:25:05.930
you know them to be a human being

00:25:05.930 --> 00:25:08.073
and they have experienced this.

00:25:10.502 --> 00:25:12.210
If that doesn't call you to action,

00:25:12.210 --> 00:25:15.293
then you gotta ask yourself what would.

00:25:20.630 --> 00:25:21.463
You know,

00:25:21.463 --> 00:25:23.210
for someone who was worried about...

00:25:25.960 --> 00:25:27.130
Earlier you were telling me,

00:25:27.130 --> 00:25:28.790
well I'm worried about...

00:25:28.790 --> 00:25:30.810
Had some trepidation
about coming on the show,

00:25:30.810 --> 00:25:34.540
because all these professional speakers

00:25:34.540 --> 00:25:39.540
on racial strife and
scholars have been talking,

00:25:41.150 --> 00:25:42.880
and I don't know what my place is.

00:25:42.880 --> 00:25:47.440
And your fears were not valid

00:25:49.710 --> 00:25:51.960
because everything...

00:25:51.960 --> 00:25:54.690
You've just talked about your experience

00:25:54.690 --> 00:25:58.470
and it's as powerful as
anything I've heard this week.

00:25:58.470 --> 00:26:00.060
So,

00:26:00.060 --> 00:26:01.713
I really do appreciate it.

00:26:05.293 --> 00:26:07.363
And I'm hoping...

00:26:10.840 --> 00:26:12.810
I would like to be optimistic.

00:26:12.810 --> 00:26:13.910
I don't know if you are,

00:26:13.910 --> 00:26:15.160
but I would like to have...

00:26:15.160 --> 00:26:19.040
I always describe myself
as a 51% optimist.

00:26:19.040 --> 00:26:21.140
I'm aware I'm pessimistic,

00:26:21.140 --> 00:26:24.500
but I wanna slightly
lean towards optimism.

00:26:24.500 --> 00:26:25.510
And I wanna hope

00:26:26.750 --> 00:26:29.360
that it gets us to a better place

00:26:29.360 --> 00:26:31.030
if we keep doing the work.

00:26:31.030 --> 00:26:31.863
I think so.

00:26:31.863 --> 00:26:33.380
I think we have to keep doing the work.

00:26:33.380 --> 00:26:34.583
I think like going back,

00:26:37.710 --> 00:26:40.260
there's no quick fix to anything.

00:26:40.260 --> 00:26:41.093
You know what?

00:26:41.093 --> 00:26:43.430
2008 we watched Barack Obama

00:26:43.430 --> 00:26:44.930
and everybody patted
themselves on the back.

00:26:44.930 --> 00:26:45.840
We're like, yes, we did it.

00:26:45.840 --> 00:26:47.563
We fixed racism. We got 'em.

00:26:47.563 --> 00:26:48.396
(clapping hands)

00:26:48.396 --> 00:26:49.855
That's done, on the next case.

00:26:49.855 --> 00:26:50.688
(laughing)

00:26:50.688 --> 00:26:52.324
And we were done with it.

00:26:52.324 --> 00:26:54.840
And then nobody went to
vote two years later,

00:26:54.840 --> 00:26:56.583
nobody went to do it.

00:26:57.710 --> 00:27:00.270
So then we need to educate ourselves

00:27:00.270 --> 00:27:02.960
on how the government works.

00:27:02.960 --> 00:27:06.150
So you don't put this all on one person,

00:27:06.150 --> 00:27:08.300
you have to work the system.

00:27:08.300 --> 00:27:10.140
And if the more we educate ourselves,

00:27:10.140 --> 00:27:11.230
the more we can see.

00:27:11.230 --> 00:27:12.370
And there's hope out there.

00:27:12.370 --> 00:27:14.263
We have to vote.

00:27:15.270 --> 00:27:17.603
We have to become a part of this.

00:27:18.540 --> 00:27:20.913
And we can see we can change things.

00:27:21.820 --> 00:27:24.480
Like the first black woman mayor

00:27:24.480 --> 00:27:25.930
was just elected in Ferguson.

00:27:26.950 --> 00:27:28.050
Just happened.

00:27:28.050 --> 00:27:30.910
We can make change happen.

00:27:30.910 --> 00:27:32.633
We just have to do it.

00:27:33.657 --> 00:27:34.850
And we can't be discouraged by voting.

00:27:34.850 --> 00:27:35.820
And yes,

00:27:35.820 --> 00:27:37.713
voter suppression is real.

00:27:38.940 --> 00:27:41.130
Gerrymandering of districts is real.

00:27:41.130 --> 00:27:42.730
These things are real.

00:27:42.730 --> 00:27:45.280
But with overwhelming numbers,

00:27:45.280 --> 00:27:46.523
you can't deny them.

00:27:47.836 --> 00:27:48.669
And you say like,

00:27:48.669 --> 00:27:51.173
you talk about getting discouraged.

00:27:53.292 --> 00:27:54.180
I can't get discouraged.

00:27:54.180 --> 00:27:55.327
Black people have been going through this

00:27:55.327 --> 00:27:57.140
for 400 years here.

00:27:57.140 --> 00:27:58.860
We haven't been discouraged yet.

00:27:58.860 --> 00:28:01.933
So I say my white friends,

00:28:03.250 --> 00:28:04.660
y'all can't either.

00:28:04.660 --> 00:28:07.290
Yeah. (laughing)

00:28:07.290 --> 00:28:08.844
But I'm discouraged.

00:28:08.844 --> 00:28:09.677
(both laughing)

00:28:09.677 --> 00:28:10.510
Oh yeah?

00:28:10.510 --> 00:28:11.518
(both laughing)

00:28:11.518 --> 00:28:13.199
This looks pretty lame.

00:28:13.199 --> 00:28:14.373
I am discouraged.

00:28:16.670 --> 00:28:18.817
Sam has to cheer Conan up tonight.

00:28:18.817 --> 00:28:21.484
(both laughing)

00:28:22.520 --> 00:28:25.813
Don't miss segment of the week.

00:28:25.813 --> 00:28:26.646
Sam,

00:28:26.646 --> 00:28:27.950
you're a really good friend

00:28:27.950 --> 00:28:29.030
and a great human being.

00:28:29.030 --> 00:28:30.496
And thank you very much

00:28:30.496 --> 00:28:33.500
for sharing with me.

00:28:33.500 --> 00:28:35.460
And for making...

00:28:35.460 --> 00:28:36.503
I'll tell you this,

00:28:37.855 --> 00:28:38.930
I feel better.

00:28:38.930 --> 00:28:40.380
Not that that's the goal,

00:28:40.380 --> 00:28:41.330
but I do.

00:28:41.330 --> 00:28:44.470
Just having you in my life.

00:28:44.470 --> 00:28:47.710
And I really appreciate you talking to me.

00:28:47.710 --> 00:28:48.543
Well,

00:28:48.543 --> 00:28:50.420
I appreciate your friendship,

00:28:50.420 --> 00:28:52.330
and I appreciate you using this time

00:28:52.330 --> 00:28:54.470
to elevate, elevate...

00:28:54.470 --> 00:28:55.310
I appreciate,

00:28:55.310 --> 00:28:56.200
I'm gonna say that one more time.

00:28:56.200 --> 00:28:58.130
I appreciate your friendship,

00:28:58.130 --> 00:28:58.963
and I

00:28:58.963 --> 00:28:59.796
(Conan laughing)

00:28:59.796 --> 00:29:00.629
This is what I was worried about.

00:29:00.629 --> 00:29:01.767
This is what I was worried about.

00:29:01.767 --> 00:29:02.680
(Conan laughing)

00:29:02.680 --> 00:29:03.513
There it is.

00:29:03.513 --> 00:29:05.360
Right at the end.

00:29:05.360 --> 00:29:06.963
Tripped up at the finish line.

00:29:08.090 --> 00:29:09.440
So well, and you (mumbles).

00:29:09.440 --> 00:29:11.528
I think subconsciously,

00:29:11.528 --> 00:29:12.361
you were like,

00:29:12.361 --> 00:29:13.194
you know what?

00:29:13.194 --> 00:29:14.027
Conan's an ass.

00:29:14.027 --> 00:29:14.860
I can't, I can't.

00:29:14.860 --> 00:29:17.567
I almost put on a professors hat,

00:29:18.580 --> 00:29:19.470
and a monocle,

00:29:19.470 --> 00:29:20.303
and it was like,

00:29:20.303 --> 00:29:21.676
and my point is made (clapping hands).

00:29:21.676 --> 00:29:25.020
And then just dumped it into the river.

00:29:25.020 --> 00:29:27.061
Yeah. Well...

00:29:27.061 --> 00:29:31.220
But I do appreciate you
elevating Black voices.

00:29:31.220 --> 00:29:32.340
Well,

00:29:32.340 --> 00:29:33.663
let's keep it going.

00:29:34.500 --> 00:29:35.623
Let's keep it going.

00:29:39.370 --> 00:29:40.203
Again,

00:29:40.203 --> 00:29:41.036
thank you so much.

00:29:41.036 --> 00:29:44.660
And I just keep thinking
about my favorite moment.

00:29:44.660 --> 00:29:47.080
I know this is so silly
to bring up at the end.

00:29:47.080 --> 00:29:48.250
But in Ghana,

00:29:48.250 --> 00:29:50.850
visiting your mom at her house,

00:29:50.850 --> 00:29:53.113
seeing all this really cool stuff,

00:29:54.110 --> 00:29:55.455
you know the moment I'm talking about.

00:29:55.455 --> 00:29:57.410
(Sam laughing)

00:29:57.410 --> 00:29:58.910
Tribal emblems,

00:29:58.910 --> 00:30:00.773
pictures of chieftains

00:30:00.773 --> 00:30:02.760
that you're related to,

00:30:02.760 --> 00:30:04.540
proud warrior stuff,

00:30:04.540 --> 00:30:05.900
just amazing.

00:30:05.900 --> 00:30:06.870
And then going down

00:30:06.870 --> 00:30:08.260
and suddenly,

00:30:08.260 --> 00:30:09.980
a bobblehead,

00:30:09.980 --> 00:30:11.424
a funko doll.

00:30:11.424 --> 00:30:12.440
Funko pop.

00:30:12.440 --> 00:30:16.090
A funko pop doll of your
character from "Veep"

00:30:16.090 --> 00:30:17.936
is between all this.

00:30:17.936 --> 00:30:20.366
(both laughing)

00:30:20.366 --> 00:30:22.190
And I remember that
moment just thinking like,

00:30:22.190 --> 00:30:23.370
this is so great.

00:30:23.370 --> 00:30:24.570
This is our son,

00:30:24.570 --> 00:30:27.250
has gone off and he's conquered America.

00:30:27.250 --> 00:30:28.884
This is what he's done.

00:30:28.884 --> 00:30:30.667
(microphone interference
drown out speaker) for me.

00:30:30.667 --> 00:30:31.500
All right,

00:30:31.500 --> 00:30:33.640
you take care and I'll see you very soon.

00:30:33.640 --> 00:30:34.580
All right.

00:30:34.580 --> 00:30:35.730
All right. Take care.

